From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: widen license-files to cover the statically
 linked dependencies

`license-files = ["LICENSE"]` is an explicit PEP 639 list, so it has
no default glob behind it: a `LICENSE.<dep>` dropped at the project
root for a library compiled into the extension is silently ignored.
extern/CMakeLists.txt FetchContent-pulls nanobind (BSD-3-Clause),
HiGHS (MIT) and eight of the author's own solver libraries
(optimizationtools, shape, mathoptsolverscmake, knapsacksolver,
multiplechoicesubsetsumsolver, subsetsumsolver, treesearchsolver,
localsearchsolver, columngenerationsolver; all MIT) and statically
links every one of them into the single `_packingsolver` extension
module, yet only the project's own LICENSE lands in
dist-info/licenses. scikit-build-core refuses the
SKBUILD_WHEEL_LICENSE_FILES environment override while
project.license-files is set (gotcha 590), so the list itself has to
change.

`LICENSE*` still matches only LICENSE in a clean checkout, so the
sdist is unchanged; the staged `LICENSE.<dep>` files are picked up in
the wheel build.

Upstream's own wheels carry the same gap: only LICENSE ships in
dist-info/licenses, with no notice for any of the ten statically
linked dependencies.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against fontanf/packingsolver]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 description = "A solver for geometrical packing and cutting-stock problems"
 readme = "README.md"
 license = "MIT"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]
 authors = [{ name = "Florian Fontan" }]
 requires-python = ">=3.12"
 classifiers = [
--
